.TH CHTTP_METHOD_STR 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
chttp_method_str \- give the canonical string for an HTTP method
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/chttp.h>

const char *chttp_method_str(chttp_method_t m);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
This function returns the uppercase ASCII name of a method, such as
"GET" or "POST".  CHTTP_ANY gives "ANY", although CHTTP_ANY is only a
sentinel for server routes and never a real HTTP method.  Any value
that the enum does not name gives "UNKNOWN".
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
A pointer to a static string literal.  You must not free it.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR chttp_request_create (3),
.BR chttpsvr_req_method (3)
